Senator Risa Hontiveros: Isama na rin po sana yung kaugnay na tanong, meron din bang mas mataas na rates sa mga susunod na foreign assisted projects?

6284
04:16:35,960 --> 04:16:49,280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Dahil na rin sa reputation costs kung ngayon ay hindi natin i-deliver yung obligasyon ng gobyerno sa mga government counterparts.

6285
04:16:49,280 --> 04:17:10,740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And while waiting for that, for those responses sa interpellation na ito, nais ko lang pong manifestation, Mr. President, na sinusuportahan ko po ang mungkahe ng chair na suportahan ang pagpupondo sa mga proyektong ito.

6286
04:17:10,740 --> 04:17:19,120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Dahil hindi lamang dagdag-gastos ang pag-delay sa mga proyektong ito, kundi pag-delay din nga po sa benepisyong sana.

6287
04:17:19,280 --> 04:17:31,000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So huling paksa na lang po, Mr. President, good sponsor, katatapos lamang ng ASEAN Summit noong nakaraang linggo.

6288
04:17:31,000 --> 04:17:42,360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: May inilaan tayo noong una na 22 billion pesos at kalaunan gumastos ng 12 billion pesos para sa pag-host natin ng summit na ito.

6289
04:17:42,800 --> 04:17:49,000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Inaasahan kong may mga kaakibat ito na mga dagdag na commitments, dagdag na projects.

6290
04:17:49,280 --> 04:17:52,960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Dagdag na partnerships mula sa ibang mga bansa.

6291
04:17:54,280 --> 04:18:01,880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So ano-ano pong mga proyekto ang naging bunga ng pag-host natin ng ASEAN Summit, Mr. President?

6292
04:18:04,880 --> 04:18:13,160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Actually, according to DBM, Mr. President, Your Honor, as we discussed earlier, they briefed me earlier,

6293
04:18:13,640 --> 04:18:19,000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: nakatipid tayo sa pag-host, kasi 22 billion yung authorized budget, but the actual

6294
04:18:19,280 --> 04:18:22,200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: expenses only reach 11 billion.

6295
04:18:22,280 --> 04:18:22,740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ah, 11.

6296
04:18:22,960 --> 04:18:26,960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 11 lang daw yung actual. Pero 22 was the authorized.

6297
04:18:27,080 --> 04:18:27,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Opo.

6298
04:18:27,300 --> 04:18:35,740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So right now, there are commitments from different countries, just like Canada.

6299
04:18:37,080 --> 04:18:38,600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: There's a trade agreement.

6300
04:18:38,740 --> 04:18:48,760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The ASEAN, Canada, and the Philippines, Canada, free trade agreements were announced as substantially concluded with signing targeted in 2027.

6301
04:18:49,280 --> 04:18:54,600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The DOF leads negotiations on financial services and taxation-related provisions.

6302
04:18:55,420 --> 04:19:03,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Both agreements are not yet enforced, but with potential economic benefits expected to materials over the medium term.

6303
04:19:03,540 --> 04:19:12,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So yung Canada po, ma'am, Mr. President, Your Honor, Philippine-Canada, FTA, will be targeted for signing in 2027.

6304
04:19:13,720 --> 04:19:18,160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And next is the digital economy, the ASEAN Digital Economy Framework Agreement.

6305
04:19:18,160 --> 04:19:18,920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yung DEFA.

6306
04:19:19,280 --> 04:19:20,140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, and DEFA.

6307
04:19:20,140 --> 04:19:27,340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Was signed on November 14, 2026, covering digital trade, cross-border payments, and data flows.

6308
04:19:27,460 --> 04:19:36,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Its implementation could support digital trade and financial services integration subject to the entry into force and domestic implementation.

6309
04:19:37,660 --> 04:19:43,500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And last but not the least, ito po, nagkaroon sila na, of course, yung APEC Economic Leaders Meeting,

6310
04:19:44,340 --> 04:19:48,460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the Philippines-Chile Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement.

6311
04:19:49,280 --> 04:19:54,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Was signed on November 19, 2026, covering areas including financial services.

6312
04:19:55,260 --> 04:20:02,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It is expected to support trade diversification, investment with economic benefits dependent on its entry into force and implementation.

6313
04:20:03,980 --> 04:20:14,980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Nabanggit nyo, good sponsor, na kung tama yung pagkasulat ko yung DOF, Financial Services and Taxation Agreements, medium term po ito pagkakasundoan.

6314
04:20:15,060 --> 04:20:16,540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Anong taon po yung medium term?

6315
04:20:19,280 --> 04:20:22,980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: O yun ba yung DEFA, good sponsor?

6316
04:20:31,220 --> 04:20:34,280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In the estimate of the DOF security, about one to two years.

6317
04:20:34,640 --> 04:20:35,600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: One to two years po.

6318
04:20:35,820 --> 04:20:36,680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: One to two years.

6319
04:20:37,380 --> 04:20:40,180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, 2027 or hanggang 2028.

6320
04:20:40,740 --> 04:20:47,380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And marami po akong narinig sa sagot nyo, good sponsor, Mr. President, na financial services.

6321
04:20:47,380 --> 04:20:49,260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Meron din po ba sa mga...

6322
04:20:49,260 --> 04:20:57,860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na buong agreements, partnerships na ito tungkol sa agrikultura at tungkol sa manufacturing din, Mr. President.

6323
04:21:03,960 --> 04:21:07,760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That was not one of the strategic priorities, Madam.

6324
04:21:09,260 --> 04:21:12,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Your Honor, Mr. President, according to our DOF Secretary.

6325
04:21:13,320 --> 04:21:15,640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Medyo nakakagulat po at sayang naman.

6326
04:21:16,120 --> 04:21:19,240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Lalo na kung kahit dito sa budget process, nakatutok tayo.

6327
04:21:19,260 --> 04:21:26,260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sa mga productive na mga programa, activities, proyekto.

6328
04:21:27,000 --> 04:21:35,580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sayang naman kung hindi sinamantala yung pagkakataon ng pag-host natin at bilang chair ng ASEAN

6329
04:21:35,580 --> 04:21:44,180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para makabuo ng ganyang klaseng mga agreements at partnerships sa maraming bansa na dumalo dito sa atin.

6330
04:21:44,300 --> 04:21:46,900
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Lalo na yung nasa pareho nating regyon.

6331
04:21:46,900 --> 04:21:48,900
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And I say this...

6332
04:21:49,260 --> 04:21:50,300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, good sponsor.

6333
04:21:50,920 --> 04:21:56,560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, Mr. President, Your Honor, according to our economic managers,

6334
04:21:57,260 --> 04:22:05,260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: what became priority issues, energy, of course, because of the Middle East crisis,

6335
04:22:05,820 --> 04:22:16,060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and that digitalization, and last but not the least, the regional security because of the West Philippine Sea issue.

6336
04:22:16,060 --> 04:22:17,480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mr. President, Your Honor.

6337
04:22:17,920 --> 04:22:18,780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Of course.

6338
04:22:19,260 --> 04:22:19,800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Good sponsor.

6339
04:22:20,120 --> 04:22:32,720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Napaka-importante ng regional security and energy, digitalization, bahagi na rin ng industry and services sector natin.

6340
04:22:32,720 --> 04:22:48,020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I'm just saying na sana mas minaksimize pa yung partnership on yung mga investments, yung mga programs na hinahanap natin dito rin sa ating budget instrument.

6341
04:22:48,020 --> 04:23:00,860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At kaya ko po itinanong ito, yung huling tanong ko, Mr. President, good sponsor, dahil kongkretong mga plano na may pondo at malino na mga deadlines ang hinahanap ng ating mga mamamayan.

6342
04:23:01,600 --> 04:23:13,220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Magandang pagkakataon yung binanggit nyo, good sponsor, na DEFA, kung totoong magkakaroon ng mga bagong suki ang mga Pilipinong MSMEs sa loob ng ASEAN.

6343
04:23:14,180 --> 04:23:18,000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Inaasahan ko na dapat may upskilling ng mga may-ari ng negosyo.

6344
04:23:18,000 --> 04:23:28,080
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At mga manggagawa, abot kaya at mabilis na internet. At may tuloy-tuloy na suporta din para sa mga negosyanteng gustong mag-export.

6345
04:23:28,680 --> 04:23:37,960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kasi gusto natin maging mas productive sa agricultural at manufacturing sectors natin, mag-generate ng surplus dyan.

6346
04:23:37,960 --> 04:23:47,960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At may export natin para nga maging mas healthy din yung ating balance of trade. Ito ang ilan sa ating kinakailangan para ma-maximize ito ng Pilipinas.

6347
04:23:48,000 --> 04:23:49,840
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At ng industriyang Pilipino.

6348
04:23:50,360 --> 04:23:53,400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ma'am, regarding ano, can we go back yung poong may information na yun?

6349
04:23:53,460 --> 04:23:54,560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, please. Salamat.

6350
04:23:54,600 --> 04:23:55,340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung poong babalikan natin.

6351
04:23:55,380 --> 04:23:55,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Opo.

6352
04:23:56,000 --> 04:24:05,220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, according to our economic managers that delays in public infra projects have contributed to the slowdown in economic growth.

6353
04:24:05,960 --> 04:24:14,780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Public construction delays reduce GDP growth by 0.5 percentage point in third quarter 2026.

6354
04:24:14,780 --> 04:24:17,780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And by 1.6 percentage in the...

6355
04:24:18,000 --> 04:24:20,460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: First three quarters of 2026.

6356
04:24:20,720 --> 04:24:26,180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, ito po yung mga naging effect to the GDP growth.

6357
04:24:27,440 --> 04:24:37,280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, pag sinuma po natin good sponsor, so, naitala na reduction by 2.1% over these four quarters this year.

6358
04:24:37,280 --> 04:24:47,960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At kung gamitin natin yung per percentage point, bawas ng 38.8 billion.

6359
04:24:47,960 --> 04:24:55,240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, sa dalawang percentage point na nabawas ngayong taon, ano na po yun?

6360
04:24:55,380 --> 04:25:04,960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Forgone revenue na or profit for the national economy na mga 76 billion pesos.

6361
04:25:10,960 --> 04:25:16,960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: According to Secretary Balisakan, the growth should be about

6362
04:25:17,960 --> 04:25:20,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 4.1%, Your Honor, Mr. President.

6363
04:25:21,900 --> 04:25:23,500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In the first three quarters.

6364
04:25:24,360 --> 04:25:25,640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Of this year, Mr.

6365
04:25:26,420 --> 04:25:27,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: This year, Mr. President.

6366
04:25:27,300 --> 04:25:28,720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: It should have been 4.3.

6367
04:25:30,120 --> 04:25:31,020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 4.1.

6368
04:25:31,340 --> 04:25:32,500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: 4.1.

6369
04:25:34,080 --> 04:25:35,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Instead of 2.5.

6370
04:25:36,120 --> 04:25:36,500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay.

6371
04:25:36,740 --> 04:25:39,240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, halos na kalahati talaga, Mr. Chair.

6372
04:25:39,240 --> 04:25:47,860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, mukhang sa pagdatapos ko ng pag-interpolate at maraming salamat, good sponsor, Mr. President, sa pagsagot.

6373
04:25:47,960 --> 04:26:03,140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mukhang marami na tayong mapapait at mahalagang leksyon ngayong taon na siguro we can't do things the same way next year.

6374
04:26:03,620 --> 04:26:05,700
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Tapos, aasa tayo ng ibang resulta.

6375
04:26:07,100 --> 04:26:13,280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, common sense lang, meron talaga tayong kailangan baguhin sa ating economic playbook.

6376
04:26:13,280 --> 04:26:17,780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And, umaasa po ako at nagko-commit sa chair na,

6377
04:26:17,960 --> 04:26:22,600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pagsikapan dito sa loob nitong budget instrument,

6378
04:26:22,840 --> 04:26:27,000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: i-reflect na yung ilang mga pagbabago sa economic playbook na ito

6379
04:26:27,000 --> 04:26:31,740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para maka-generate tayo ng ibang resulta sa susunod na taon.

6380
04:26:32,220 --> 04:26:38,880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Dahil kung hindi, kung magmamatigas po tayo na gawin pa rin yung ginawa natin itong taon,

6381
04:26:38,880 --> 04:26:41,800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na nag-generate ng ganitong mga resulta,

6382
04:26:41,900 --> 04:26:45,880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ang ating mga government economic managers na mismo ang nag-ulat sa atin,

6383
04:26:46,820 --> 04:26:47,880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: eh di wala tayong aasalan.

6384
04:26:47,960 --> 04:26:49,300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kundi more of the same.

6385
04:26:49,640 --> 04:26:53,600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And worse, dahil patuloy pa rin yung gera sa labas,

6386
04:26:54,780 --> 04:26:58,580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: patuloy pa rin unpredictable yung presyo ng langis,

6387
04:26:59,680 --> 04:27:02,080
Senator Risa Hontiveros: andiyan pa yung super El Niño na nakaamba.

6388
04:27:02,800 --> 04:27:07,660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But if we also learn not just the negative lessons na nararanasan natin,

6389
04:27:07,720 --> 04:27:11,380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: but the positive lessons doon naman sa ating mga kapitbahay,

6390
04:27:11,840 --> 04:27:13,120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pag iniba po natin,

6391
04:27:50,040 --> 04:27:57,700
Senator Risa Hontiveros: din sa ating mga kababayan na makipagtulungan po tayong lahat sa ganitong ilang mga bagong pamamaraan

6392
04:27:57,700 --> 04:28:04,800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para maiwasan yung stagflation at makaahon sa kasalukuyang pagdurusa ng ating mga kababayan

6393
04:28:04,800 --> 04:28:12,840
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at palakasin na, pagyamanin na yung ating ekonomiya at yung lahat ng mga kababayan natin

6394
04:28:12,840 --> 04:28:14,980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: simula na sa mga pinaka-vulnerable.

6395
04:28:14,980 --> 04:28:21,580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Maraming salamat po, good sponsor sa ating mga government economic managers. Salamat po, Mr. President.

6396
04:28:23,700 --> 04:28:27,260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Tiberas. Thank you, Mr. President.

6397
04:28:29,400 --> 04:28:31,260
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, Mr. President, thank you.

6398
04:28:31,780 --> 04:28:42,340
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mr. President, next to propounder questions at this juncture is the distinguished lady from the city of Taguig and Pateros,

6399
04:28:42,340 --> 04:28:46,860
Senator Joel Villanueva: no other than Senator Pia Cayetano. I move that she be recognized, Mr. President.

6400
04:28:48,200 --> 04:28:50,020
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Senator Pia Cayetano is recognized.

6401
04:29:12,340 --> 04:29:16,600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you, Mr. President.

6402
04:29:19,600 --> 04:29:21,460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Good evening, Chairman. Do you need a...

6403
04:29:21,460 --> 04:29:22,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Good evening, Senator Pia.

6404
04:29:22,980 --> 04:29:26,640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think you need a standing break. Sitting is the new smoking.

6405
04:29:26,900 --> 04:29:31,020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, if you and the economic team want to stand up, I don't mind.

6406
04:29:31,200 --> 04:29:33,820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Stand up, sit down, stand up. I really don't mind.

6407
04:29:34,220 --> 04:29:36,360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Huwag lang kayo lumabas kasi yung questions ko.

6408
04:29:40,740 --> 04:29:42,200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I mean it. I don't know why no one's listening.

6409
04:29:42,340 --> 04:29:46,260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: You should really stand up. It's not good for your health. Thank you.

6410
04:29:47,600 --> 04:29:49,060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'm just looking out for your health.

6411
04:29:50,300 --> 04:29:53,280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, should I proceed? Mr. Chairman, are you okay?

6412
04:29:53,520 --> 04:29:55,280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, we're okay.

6413
04:29:55,580 --> 04:29:59,260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, thank you so much. I don't think I will be that long.

6414
04:30:00,000 --> 04:30:03,640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I tried to listen to the questions of our colleagues.

6415
04:30:03,780 --> 04:30:06,520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: A lot of us have some common interests and concerns, no?

6416
04:30:06,580 --> 04:30:10,500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Senator Riza, earlier Senator Allan, our other colleagues.

6417
04:30:10,740 --> 04:30:15,200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I may only repeat them in the sense that they're like follow-up questions.

6418
04:30:15,420 --> 04:30:16,780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I'll start with Phil Health.

6419
04:30:18,400 --> 04:30:21,200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Chairman, alam mo na ang tatanungin ko dito.

6420
04:30:21,900 --> 04:30:22,420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Alam mo na.

6421
04:30:22,420 --> 04:30:33,680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And my statement will start with, I'd like to thank the chairperson because

6422
04:30:33,680 --> 04:30:41,480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: my interpolation won't be as harsh as it would be if not for the chairman's intervention.

6423
04:30:41,760 --> 04:30:43,580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, this is about the syntax funding.

6424
04:30:44,320 --> 04:30:51,020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I knew when I wrote the chairman that the syntax deficiency for 2019,

6425
04:30:51,020 --> 04:30:52,400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I knew that he wouldn't.

6426
04:30:52,420 --> 04:30:56,660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I knew that he would look into every possibility to fund it.

6427
04:30:56,840 --> 04:30:57,900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And thank you, Mr. Chairman.

6428
04:30:57,980 --> 04:30:58,860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I know it's not an easy job.

6429
04:30:58,960 --> 04:31:07,020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: You produced 19 billion pesos to fund the Phil Health deficit in the sense that

6430
04:31:07,020 --> 04:31:09,620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: it should have been in the NEP and it was not in the NEP.

6431
04:31:10,220 --> 04:31:13,160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And you found a way to fund this.

6432
04:31:13,260 --> 04:31:16,040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, thank you so much for that, Mr. Chairman.

6433
04:31:16,040 --> 04:31:22,040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I still really need this not to be the problem of the legislature.

6434
04:31:22,420 --> 04:31:27,800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I will go back to the hearing held just a few months ago in August

6435
04:31:27,800 --> 04:31:33,700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: when I asked the DBM Secretary who was very new at that time.

6436
04:31:33,820 --> 04:31:41,380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I was quite lenient naman po with the need of the Secretary to find out what's going on.

6437
04:31:41,440 --> 04:31:44,500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I said, why is this not in the NEP?

6438
04:31:44,500 --> 04:31:52,320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: This is an earmarked fund that every year, I along with other colleagues like Senator Loren and Senator JV,

6439
04:31:52,420 --> 04:31:53,860
