6988
05:05:51,160 --> 05:05:51,700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Good question.

6989
05:05:52,160 --> 05:05:53,420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, year on year.

6990
05:05:53,720 --> 05:05:55,020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, zero from 2025.

6991
05:05:56,220 --> 05:05:57,020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We're in the last quarter.

6992
05:05:57,020 --> 05:06:03,460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, what was it from 2025, fourth quarter, compared to 2024?

6993
05:06:04,420 --> 05:06:05,360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yun, may growth pa yun?

6994
05:06:06,520 --> 05:06:09,700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'm trying to remember kasi when did our luck turn so bad?

6995
05:06:10,640 --> 05:06:18,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: According to them, according to the economic managers, yes, there's growth during those periods.

6996
05:06:18,840 --> 05:06:19,940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What was the growth rate?

6997
05:06:20,260 --> 05:06:20,680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Do we know?

6998
05:06:21,340 --> 05:06:21,820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Do we recall?

6999
05:06:21,940 --> 05:06:22,920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Can we quickly check lang?

7000
05:06:23,980 --> 05:06:24,340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Like one.

7001
05:06:52,380 --> 05:06:55,900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And while they're looking for more details to provide,

7002
05:06:56,940 --> 05:06:58,700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Can we just compare ourselves with our neighbors?

7003
05:06:58,960 --> 05:07:03,220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: In the third quarter of this year, Vietnam's economy expanded by 9.95%,

7004
05:07:03,220 --> 05:07:04,900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: almost 10% year on year,

7005
05:07:05,340 --> 05:07:08,160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: nearly twice the rate recorded by Indonesia, Singapore, and Malaysia,

7006
05:07:08,440 --> 05:07:10,680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: which all grew by around 5%.

7007
05:07:10,680 --> 05:07:13,800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So we lag last.

7008
05:07:14,360 --> 05:07:18,340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So sad for us.

7009
05:07:20,900 --> 05:07:26,480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The difference is Vietnam concentrated really in developing

7010
05:07:26,480 --> 05:07:30,120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: their industries, especially the export industry.

7011
05:07:31,360 --> 05:07:33,380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But we revised CREATE again.

7012
05:07:33,900 --> 05:07:35,260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I was the author of CREATE,

7013
05:07:36,120 --> 05:07:41,840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: which was a pandemic law that I worked on.

7014
05:07:42,480 --> 05:07:46,960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then under this administration, CREATE agad nirevise.

7015
05:07:46,960 --> 05:07:48,680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So did it bring results?

7016
05:07:50,320 --> 05:07:55,000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: According to the RDIF Secretary, that export is up last.

7017
05:07:56,480 --> 05:08:00,060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But this year, it's about 16%.

7018
05:08:00,060 --> 05:08:01,640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sorry, what was it?

7019
05:08:02,220 --> 05:08:03,780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Last year, it was 30%.

7020
05:08:03,780 --> 05:08:08,240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Do we know why?

7021
05:08:08,380 --> 05:08:12,600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I mean, is it like one or two major buyers that ang mas magaling na seller?

7022
05:08:13,880 --> 05:08:14,700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ano kaya yung reason?

7023
05:08:15,220 --> 05:08:18,660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Para we know who to ask when the other agencies come here, di ba, Mr. Chairman?

7024
05:08:18,860 --> 05:08:21,020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Like if it's DTI ba tatanungin namin?

7025
05:08:21,180 --> 05:08:22,340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: DA ba tatanungin namin?

7026
05:08:23,440 --> 05:08:23,880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yeah.

7027
05:08:24,160 --> 05:08:25,340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What industry?

7028
05:08:25,660 --> 05:08:25,920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yeah.

7029
05:08:26,480 --> 05:08:41,220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I already have the information asked earlier, Your Honor.

7030
05:08:41,220 --> 05:08:50,460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: For manufacturing for 2025, there's a 2.8% growth first quarter to third quarter.

7031
05:08:51,380 --> 05:08:54,220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Same period, 2026, 1.3%.

7032
05:08:54,820 --> 05:08:56,440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: First quarter.

7033
05:08:56,480 --> 05:09:03,840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In industry, 2025, 2.5% for the first three quarters.

7034
05:09:04,700 --> 05:09:14,820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In same period, 2026, it's now minus 0.8% for the whole industry, for three quarters, Your Honor.

7035
05:09:14,940 --> 05:09:18,380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So nag-negative na siya for 2026, yung industry.

7036
05:09:20,780 --> 05:09:23,560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sorry, is this the manufacturing industry?

7037
05:09:24,560 --> 05:09:25,520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Is that what we're talking about?

7038
05:09:25,520 --> 05:09:26,320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What are we talking about?

7039
05:09:26,480 --> 05:09:28,480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Let's see.

7040
05:09:29,960 --> 05:09:35,680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung in the, this is yung total po of the industry is about negative 0.8%.

7041
05:09:35,680 --> 05:09:36,740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sorry, I'm lost.

7042
05:09:36,820 --> 05:09:38,260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What do you mean by total of the industry?

7043
05:09:38,460 --> 05:09:38,920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What, what industry?

7044
05:09:39,000 --> 05:09:39,960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Manufacturing is part of.

7045
05:09:40,320 --> 05:09:41,880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Manufacturing is part of?

7046
05:09:42,100 --> 05:09:44,340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It's part of the industry, of the whole industry.

7047
05:09:45,700 --> 05:09:46,640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ah, can you be?

7048
05:09:46,640 --> 05:09:48,860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: May ba pang industry, it's not just manufacturing.

7049
05:09:49,980 --> 05:09:52,720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Agri, construction.

7050
05:09:52,720 --> 05:09:54,960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So they included everything.

7051
05:09:55,320 --> 05:09:55,780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mining.

7052
05:09:56,480 --> 05:10:01,260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So manufacturing is the biggest part of the industry.

7053
05:10:01,560 --> 05:10:02,320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Can I have a copy?

7054
05:10:02,860 --> 05:10:03,280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Can we just?

7055
05:10:03,400 --> 05:10:04,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, they will provide, Your Honor.

7056
05:10:04,640 --> 05:10:08,940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sana ngayon kasi para I can ask more intelligent questions.

7057
05:10:09,200 --> 05:10:09,600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you.

7058
05:10:09,600 --> 05:10:09,640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you.

7059
05:10:16,900 --> 05:10:21,220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So you mentioned, Your Honor, Vietnam focused on export, no?

7060
05:10:22,200 --> 05:10:26,400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So what about, I know Singapore is very different from us, but I don't know, Indonesia,

7061
05:10:26,480 --> 05:10:32,100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Malaysia, naka-5% pa rin sila, anumang pinagkaiba natin?

7062
05:10:37,560 --> 05:10:41,720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I mean, it's the first thing I do, I look at, I look at similarly-situated.

7063
05:10:46,920 --> 05:10:54,860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Well, the difference, Your Honor, Mr. President, that Indonesia has refinery, oil, refined oil,

7064
05:10:54,860 --> 05:10:56,360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and then Malaysia.

7065
05:10:56,360 --> 05:11:03,680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thailand, although almost the same GDP growth as us, has tourism.

7066
05:11:04,360 --> 05:11:06,880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So yun po yung ma-advantage po nung neighbors natin.

7067
05:11:09,680 --> 05:11:12,340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So doon na lang tayo, magbalik na naman tayo sa tourism.

7068
05:11:13,440 --> 05:11:15,600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Tanong tayo bukas sa tourism.

7069
05:11:15,600 --> 05:11:16,600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I think even tourism is...

7070
05:11:18,400 --> 05:11:23,700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, well, anyway, our colleagues are also looking at these numbers.

7071
05:11:23,860 --> 05:11:25,340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Maybe they'll also ask some questions.

7072
05:11:26,360 --> 05:11:34,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mr. President, if I may, just a quick interjection on this particular topic.

7073
05:11:34,740 --> 05:11:43,760
Senator Joel Villanueva: I have been monitoring the employment rate, underemployment rate for quite some time,

7074
05:11:43,760 --> 05:11:54,760
Senator Joel Villanueva: and I'm just a bit, well, to say the least, alarmed to hear that there's zero increase

7075
05:11:54,760 --> 05:11:55,760
Senator Joel Villanueva: in the...

7076
05:11:56,360 --> 05:11:57,360
Senator Joel Villanueva: manufacturing sector.

7077
05:11:57,360 --> 05:11:58,360
Senator Joel Villanueva: It's not...

7078
05:11:58,360 --> 05:12:04,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: Did I hear it right, Mr. President, distinguished chairperson?

7079
05:12:04,000 --> 05:12:14,640
Senator Joel Villanueva: Because it's kind of weird that we actually put in, when you talk about key employment

7080
05:12:14,640 --> 05:12:23,400
Senator Joel Villanueva: generation sectors, not only construction, not only semiconductors,

7081
05:12:23,400 --> 05:12:26,700
Senator Joel Villanueva: call center industry,

7082
05:12:26,700 --> 05:12:29,720
Senator Joel Villanueva: More importantly, manufacturing is part of it.

7083
05:12:29,720 --> 05:12:35,320
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I can see Secretary Balisacan, who is also the chairperson of our Trabajo Para sa Dayan

7084
05:12:35,320 --> 05:12:36,320
Senator Joel Villanueva: Council.

7085
05:12:36,320 --> 05:12:41,080
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, I'm just wondering, did they hear it right, Mr. President?

7086
05:12:41,080 --> 05:12:50,400
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I was looking attentively with the note that was passed on to Senator Pia on the manufacturing

7087
05:12:50,400 --> 05:12:51,500
Senator Joel Villanueva: growth.

7088
05:12:51,500 --> 05:12:55,080
Senator Joel Villanueva: And then, it says here, industry.

7089
05:12:55,080 --> 05:13:21,300
Senator Joel Villanueva: So what industry is this? I actually have no idea what this is because it says here manufacturing 2025, 2.7%, 2026, 1.3 or 1.8% and then industry. I don't know the difference. So I was actually confused looking at this particular note that was passed on to Senator Pia. Can we be clarified on that, Your Honor, Mr. Chairman?

7090
05:13:25,080 --> 05:13:55,060
Senator Joel Villanueva: Can we be clarified on that, Your Honor?

7091
05:13:55,080 --> 05:14:25,060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Can we be clarified on that, Your Honor?

7092
05:14:25,080 --> 05:14:38,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But the problem is unemployed, Tomas, then. So from 2.07, 2025, it became 2.72 in 2026.

7093
05:14:39,840 --> 05:14:49,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, but that's when you calculate the increase of employment versus the increase of unemployment.

7094
05:14:49,120 --> 05:14:55,060
Senator Joel Villanueva: But when you talk about the previous year of those who are employed in that particular,

7095
05:14:55,080 --> 05:14:59,980
Senator Joel Villanueva: in that particular, for example, manufacturing industry.

7096
05:15:00,620 --> 05:15:05,740
Senator Joel Villanueva: Lumago po, ginong Pangulo. Nag-increase po. Is that correct, Mr. President?

7097
05:15:05,840 --> 05:15:07,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, lumago naman.

7098
05:15:08,040 --> 05:15:11,980
Senator Joel Villanueva: I just wanted to be clarified because again, Mr. President,

7099
05:15:12,860 --> 05:15:19,240
Senator Joel Villanueva: we, as mentioned a while ago by Senator Pia, we have been passing laws and later on I will bring it up.

7100
05:15:19,500 --> 05:15:23,260
Senator Joel Villanueva: We have been passing laws pero hindi naman na napopondohan.

7101
05:15:23,720 --> 05:15:28,900
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kung napondohan man, God knows kung paano na i-implement

7102
05:15:28,900 --> 05:15:33,660
Senator Joel Villanueva: because masakit ho sa pandinig na you worked so hard for this,

7103
05:15:33,660 --> 05:15:38,460
Senator Joel Villanueva: the very first administration in the history of this country

7104
05:15:38,460 --> 05:15:45,760
Senator Joel Villanueva: that came up with a blueprint of a employment roadmap

7105
05:15:45,760 --> 05:15:52,740
Senator Joel Villanueva: na ipinasaho ng kongresong ito, pinutukan natin, pinondohan at pinututukan

7106
05:15:52,740 --> 05:15:57,380
Senator Joel Villanueva: and then you will hear na there's zero increase in employment.

7107
05:15:57,680 --> 05:15:58,780
Senator Joel Villanueva: Hindi ko kasi talaga maganda.

7108
05:15:58,900 --> 05:16:04,300
Senator Joel Villanueva: So maraming salamat sa ating chairperson na nilinaw po, Mr. President.

7109
05:16:04,740 --> 05:16:11,700
Senator Joel Villanueva: Tumataas yung unemployment pero yung employment po doon sa particular industry dito sa manufacturing sector

7110
05:16:11,700 --> 05:16:16,580
Senator Joel Villanueva: nag-increase naman po, lumago po, nagkaroon po ng bagong employment.

7111
05:16:16,760 --> 05:16:17,560
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Mr. President.

7112
05:16:19,460 --> 05:16:20,700
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Senator Pia.

7113
05:16:20,880 --> 05:16:21,360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you.

7114
05:16:22,360 --> 05:16:26,740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'll go to another topic, Mr. President, Mr. Chairman.

7115
05:16:28,900 --> 05:16:34,940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: In the last SONA, the President said, well, ordered na tanggalin na yung systems laws

7116
05:16:34,940 --> 05:16:37,160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: na kinakarga ng mga consumers.

7117
05:16:38,220 --> 05:16:45,600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So because I handled the budget of DOE, ERC, NEA, and the like,

7118
05:16:46,320 --> 05:16:51,020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: sabi ni DOE, wala na siyang ibang hihingi na budgetary amendment,

7119
05:16:51,020 --> 05:16:58,820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: except, budgetary request, except to support NEA's request for 10 billion,

7120
05:16:58,900 --> 05:17:07,180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: which, according to NEA, will be used directly to implement these instructions of the President,

7121
05:17:07,580 --> 05:17:11,660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: which is nga, tanggalin na yung systems laws na karga ng mga tao.

7122
05:17:12,360 --> 05:17:19,200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, simply put, NEA intends to grant loans to electric cooperatives,

7123
05:17:19,640 --> 05:17:24,900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and the average amount is 25 million per cooperative, to put up metering systems.

7124
05:17:24,900 --> 05:17:27,900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, the Chairman...

7125
05:17:28,900 --> 05:17:32,400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Obviously, was not able to find funding for this na, no?

7126
05:17:32,580 --> 05:17:34,820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Alam ko, ang dami-dami talagang nagre-request eh.

7127
05:17:35,100 --> 05:17:42,500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I'm just saying, Mr. President, na this is a specific instruction of the President,

7128
05:17:42,940 --> 05:17:48,180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and so, I don't know if the economic team has any input on this,

7129
05:17:48,280 --> 05:17:52,740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: kasi sila naman ang kinukonsulta ng Presidente when he comes up with his statements.

7130
05:17:53,080 --> 05:17:58,460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, now, when I talk to NEA, and I promise them that I will do whatever I can,

7131
05:17:58,900 --> 05:18:03,700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: because all over the country, ang dami-dami pa rin brown-out.

7132
05:18:03,820 --> 05:18:07,180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I mean, tayong mga taga-Manila, hindi natin masyado nararamdaman yan.

7133
05:18:07,760 --> 05:18:11,940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero sa province, and Senator JV, like me, has friends from all over,

7134
05:18:12,680 --> 05:18:20,280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: they live with this, you know, unreliable electricity, intermittent brown-outs,

7135
05:18:20,280 --> 05:18:25,840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: the need to purchase, ang tawag dito, yung generators.

7136
05:18:27,060 --> 05:18:28,280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, now, NEA...

7137
05:18:28,900 --> 05:18:34,160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, NEA is requesting for, they intend to implement this in a staggered way.

7138
05:18:34,400 --> 05:18:43,600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, that is my task to help them find some kind of support for this, Mr. President.

7139
05:18:43,720 --> 05:18:48,640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I'm bringing this to the attention of NEDA, because instructions nga ito ng Presidente.

7140
05:18:49,180 --> 05:18:56,920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, pag sinabing, oh, hindi pinasaya ng Congress, well, alam ko na wala yan sa NEP.

7141
05:18:56,920 --> 05:18:57,620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Wala sa NEP.

7142
05:18:57,780 --> 05:18:58,740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi nga, by the time...

7143
05:18:58,900 --> 05:19:00,920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That SONA was delivered, wala pang NEP.

7144
05:19:01,280 --> 05:19:03,920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But, so, who's gonna look for the funding for this?

7145
05:19:10,460 --> 05:19:15,800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And this matters, because these are the small entrepreneurs, the MSMEs,

7146
05:19:15,800 --> 05:19:19,980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: that are all over the province, nahirap-nahirap sa negosyo nilang, walang kuryente,

7147
05:19:20,500 --> 05:19:25,960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: mga nanay na hindi man lang matutur yung anak nila, dahil mawawala ng kuryente ng maaga.

7148
05:19:28,900 --> 05:19:34,240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yung mga negosyo, masisiraan ng pagkain na nasa REF, dahil walang kuryente.

7149
05:21:33,420 --> 05:21:41,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Your Honor, Mr. President, according to Secretary, DOF Secretary, the Economic Managers,

7150
05:21:41,420 --> 05:21:42,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: it's an important issue.

7151
05:21:42,420 --> 05:21:43,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It's really a fiscal space problem.

7152
05:21:43,420 --> 05:21:51,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Although it was the President who announced ito pong issue on the systems laws,

7153
05:21:51,420 --> 05:21:58,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: it really boils down to the available fiscal space, Your Honor, Mr. President.

7154
05:21:58,420 --> 05:22:10,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So talagang it's really that tight, Your Honor, that they cannot give an outright answer where to get.

7155
05:22:10,420 --> 05:22:11,420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So anyway, Mr. President,

7156
05:22:11,420 --> 05:22:19,420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: it's an interesting problem because according to NEA, they can solve this with funding.

7157
05:22:19,420 --> 05:22:20,420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And this is by way of loans.

7158
05:22:20,420 --> 05:22:23,420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And you know what the repayment is sa loans? Kasi I asked eh.

7159
05:22:23,420 --> 05:22:25,420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's 99%.

7160
05:22:25,420 --> 05:22:29,420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So technically, it's not technically, it is not a dole out.

7161
05:22:29,420 --> 05:22:30,420
